/target
# Beads: track ONLY the issues.jsonl checkpoint. It survives a fresh clone / db
# rebuild and is what makes beads visible to other hosts (see CLAUDE.md §6).
# Everything else under .beads/ is per-machine runtime state — the live SQLite
# store and its timestamped backups, .bf_history rotation, traces, recovery
# dirs, locks and merge artifacts — and must stay out of git.
/.beads/*
!/.beads/issues.jsonl
__pycache__/

# Backup and debug artifacts from revert/verify cycles
*.backup
*.before-revert
*.with-fixes
output_*.txt
test-outputs/

# bead-rs store: the durable artefact is the checkpoint plus config.json.
# (`beads.db` stays ignored — it is per-machine live state.)
!/.beads/checkpoint/
!/.beads/checkpoint/**
!/.beads/config.json
